{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03324",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.74,
      "end_seconds": 4.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I think it's my turn."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.4,
      "end_seconds": 9.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "no problem at all, come in. What's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 14.65,
      "end_seconds": 21.92,
      "duration_seconds": 7.27,
      "text": "doctor, I'll sit in if that's okay, I know what's been happening"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.01,
      "end_seconds": 32.01,
      "duration_seconds": 8.0,
      "text": "Mainly headaches most days. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.74,
      "end_seconds": 38.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "Right, how long has it it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.16,
      "end_seconds": 42.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "probably six months yeah"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.46,
      "end_seconds": 48.71,
      "duration_seconds": 5.25,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.38,
      "end_seconds": 54.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "I'd say moderate. Painkillers helps a a bit"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.66,
      "end_seconds": 59.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.87,
      "end_seconds": 91.29,
      "duration_seconds": 26.42,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get light sensitivity as well. Ah, the light sensitivity? That's been for three weeks. Well, and there's taking painkillers every day as well, about a month now. Yeah, uh, as for taking painkillers every day, it's moderate, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.37,
      "end_seconds": 96.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.41,
      "end_seconds": 110.84,
      "duration_seconds": 13.43,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother. I hardly move around during the day. I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.85,
      "end_seconds": 116.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.13,
      "end_seconds": 122.27,
      "duration_seconds": 5.14,
      "text": "right, um, I don't think I have any, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 123.98,
      "end_seconds": 133.82,
      "duration_seconds": 9.84,
      "text": "hmm, hold on, doctor, I think she reacted to to diclofenac once i'm not certain, though"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.87,
      "end_seconds": 138.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Um, I don't remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.94,
      "end_seconds": 146.29,
      "duration_seconds": 6.35,
      "text": "Fair enough, I'll write down both versions. Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.26,
      "end_seconds": 156.59,
      "duration_seconds": 8.33,
      "text": "Migraines, for two years. Ah, I've had an irregular heartbeat for two years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.1,
      "end_seconds": 159.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "okay, go on"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.48,
      "end_seconds": 163.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.52,
      "text": "I've got diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.01,
      "end_seconds": 175.92,
      "duration_seconds": 10.91,
      "text": "I follow. Okay, I can see migraines and diabetes in your file as well. Tell me your medicines, please. It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.71,
      "end_seconds": 179.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Propranolol, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.92,
      "end_seconds": 182.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "and what strength is that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.12,
      "end_seconds": 198.08,
      "duration_seconds": 13.96,
      "text": "40 milligrams, I think that's what's on the box. Ah, I take something called warf... warfarin, 3 milligrams, maybe, in the evening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.69,
      "end_seconds": 202.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "did you happen to bring the box or the paperwork?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.57,
      "end_seconds": 216.22,
      "duration_seconds": 11.65,
      "text": "I mean, not with me. I'll bring it next time. Gliclazide. I take it 80 milligrams, twice a day for my sugar"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 218.18,
      "end_seconds": 225.74,
      "duration_seconds": 7.56,
      "text": "It's meant to be twice a day, though I don't see she take it every time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.3,
      "end_seconds": 237.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Did you get visual changes, weakness, fever or stiff neck?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.97,
      "end_seconds": 242.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "no, I'd have said so"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.99,
      "end_seconds": 245.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Any trouble with the waterworks?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 246.18,
      "end_seconds": 248.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "No, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.29,
      "end_seconds": 259.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "I'll note down your vital signs first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.7,
      "end_seconds": 271.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.2,
      "end_seconds": 303.89,
      "duration_seconds": 10.69,
      "text": "okay: temp 36.4 degrees, SpO2 98 percent on room air, pulse is 72 beats a a minute, respiratory rate 17, BP is 123 over 70."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.95,
      "end_seconds": 309.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.42,
      "end_seconds": 312.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "Okay, breathe out slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.34,
      "end_seconds": 321.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "your neurological examination is normal"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.19,
      "end_seconds": 329.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 338.53,
      "end_seconds": 363.61,
      "duration_seconds": 25.08,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression is this: This is probably medication-overuse headache on a background of migraine. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. I'd also keep tension-type headache in mind. Let me repeat that back to make sure. You've had headaches most days for six months, moderate, and no weakness or visual changes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 364.42,
      "end_seconds": 366.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "That's what happened, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 367.75,
      "end_seconds": 384.14,
      "duration_seconds": 16.39,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. I don't need to add any tests or treatment at this point. Right, anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 385.56,
      "end_seconds": 388.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Alright, uh, thanks, take care."
    }
  ]
}